Are you also using the "Use mean scores" option? NBLAST is asymmetric. The score for a big neuron vs a small neuron may be low even if the score for a small neuron vs a big neuron is high. See the NBLAST paper for more details of this. TH-XXX neurons are likely very big with arbours across large swathes of the brain. Note that MIP search and NBLAST do different things so that it is not guaranteed that you will get the same answer. Also you should make sure to process your EM neurons by pruning twigs less than 2-5µm before making the dot props object. Best, Greg.

